## 3) Proxy Layer (governor.ts)

Goal: small TypeScript express proxy that forwards requests to LLMs or blocks based on `/enforce/check`.

Minimal Node/Express example (TypeScript):
```ts
import express from "express";
import fetch from "node-fetch"; // or undici
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());

const API_URL = "http://localhost:8000/enforce/check";

app.post("/proxy", async (req, res) => {
  const text = JSON.stringify(req.body);
  // call GovernAble enforce endpoint
  const r = await fetch(API_URL, {method:"POST", body: text, headers:{ "Content-Type":"application/json" }});
  const decision = await r.json();
  if (!decision.allowed) {
     return res.status(403).json({error: "Blocked by GovernAble", reasons: decision.reasons});
  }
  // forward to actual upstream LLM (upstream URL from config)
  // ... fetch upstream and pipe response ...
  res.json({status: "forwarded"});
});

app.listen(3000, ()=> console.log("governor running on 3000"));
```
- Integrate a simple cache for repeated checks.
- For LLM proxying, stream / chunk handling is needed (use node http/stream).

